Found the real cause: **the four custom actions were declared in the wrong place**. Every other multi-form object in this project (`fam_physical_verification`, `fam_asset_transfer`, `fam_asset_register`, `fam_asset_disposal`) puts its action buttons inside the **header form's own** `sql_model.actions[]` array, and leaves the top-level `transaction.actions[]` empty. `fam_amc_contracts` had it backwards — "Edit" was correctly in the header form's actions, but "Submit for Approval", "Approve", "Renew" and "Cancel" were misplaced at the top-level `transaction.actions[]`, which doesn't render in the 3-dot menu — so only "Edit" ever showed up.

**Fix:** moved Submit for Approval / Approve / Renew / Cancel into `sql_models[0].sql_model.actions[]` alongside Edit (matching the project's established pattern), and cleared the now-empty top-level `transaction.actions[]`.

